  "narrative": {
    "benchmark_md": "",
    "issue_register_md": "This section documents regulatory enforcement actions, supervisory findings, and material incidents that impact capability scores through the assessment's scoring methodology. All items listed have been confirmed from primary source T1 evidence (FINRA AWC documents, SEC enforcement orders, CFTC orders, state AG filings). IBKR has accumulated ~$62M+ (10 enforcement actions/incidents, 2020-2025) across the period 2020-2025, representing the most material compliance headwind in this assessment cohort. Each enforcement action is mapped to the specific capabilities it caps and the maturity ceiling that applies. The pattern finding \u2014 confirmed by multiple independent regulators \u2014 is 'automation-without-governance scope': IBKR deploys automation at extraordinary scale, but each AWC identifies a specific domain where automated processes lacked adequate scope, coverage, or supervisory oversight.",
